A||||10||XDrewX||New stereo/factory sub not working||||10||
Z||000000||XDrewX||06-05-2001||07:43 PM||||I installed a nwe stereo today, i used one of those wiring kits so i could just plug the new stereo into the existing wiring harness. Now my factory sub does not work, (it worked before) but everything else is fine.  The wiring kit did not address the sub.  Has anyone else had this problem and if so does anyone know a soultion ? ||||reg||10
Z||000001||wkayl||06-05-2001||07:50 PM||||You have too wire in a relay.  Some have hooked the Sub power direct, but this is the best way to do it.  Here is a link as to how to wire the relay.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||06-05-2001||08:24 PM||||I think you can also just wire the yellow ignition wire to the pink amp wires.  I just wired up a 100 watt amp that I picked up for free.  Sounds better, too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-05-2001||08:49 PM||||Don't bother with that relay mess. Heres an easier way to do it. On the harness you bought and wired the stereo to, you will find a (most likly) red wire, that has 12v+ power when the ignition is on. You should also find a blue remote wire. It has 12v power when your deck is on, (power comes from the deck). On the stock radio, the amp is powered off this remote wire, the stock deck puts out alot more power thru this wire that an aftermarket decks. You need to cut the blue (I think its blue, I'll make sure when I get home) wire, and strip it. Cap off the end comming from the stereo, and don't use it. The end going to the car harness is the one you want to stip. Stip about an inch of insulation off, and then take a knife and bare some off the red wire. Don't cut the red wire, just remove some insulation from it, then wrap the blue remote wire around the red wire. This will work if done correctly.<P>Like I said before, don't cut anything till I confirm that the remote wire is actually blue. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||06-05-2001||08:52 PM||||BTW, the wire that I think is blue, is also called an Auto Anntenna wire. If you just bought the harness, it should be labled, so look on the package or the wire itself.<P>Also, in reguard to the post above my first. You want to hook it to the red ignition wire, usally the yellow wire is constant 12v, so it would leave the amp on all the time and will run the battery down.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-05-2001||10:37 PM||||But the wire that powers the amp is pink. Well actually it is two pinks. I just put these in with the red key hot wire as well.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||06-05-2001||11:46 PM||||Unless you have already cut the factory harness, DON'T! I mean cut and splice the wires on the aftermarket harness you purchased and wired to the new stereo harness. The two pink wires go directly to the amp, one is actually power and the other is the amps remote on.||||reg||1
Z||000007||86seyellow||06-10-2001||10:51 PM||||WOW, i just took out the factory Sub, put in a 10" jensen mounted on front floor, wow what a feeling, running a aiwa system 2 4x10 pioneers and 2 4x6 with jensen sub. wanna rock anyone, zero distortion, to bad this isnt my everday car!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||XDrewX||06-11-2001||01:13 PM||||Thankx everyone for your help, i got it wired corectly and replaced the 4 x 10's with new kenwoods(will be replacing the 4x6 later.  My question:<P>At the volumns i listen to music at it is only a matter of time before the factory sub goes.  Does anyone know of an after market sub that will replace the stock one and will sound the same using the factory 20watt amp  ???||||reg||1
Z||000009||kslish||06-12-2001||01:53 AM||||Rodney Dickman has an aftermarket replacement subwoofer for the Fiero....see it at: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/n60.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/n60.html</A> <P>The subwoofer is a wierd size (I think it's a 5 inch, can't remember exactly) and isn't that common in the aftermarket.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||trigger||06-12-2001||03:12 PM||||The factory sub is a 5 1/4 in.  I know some people have opened up the hole, and installed a 6 1/2 in. sub.  I have a 6 1/2 in. altec lansing sub in a ported computer box, hooked up to a 75 watt amp and it hits pretty hard.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
